# Frontend Specific Rules

- Use React.js for building UI components.
- Use Babylon.js for 3D rendering.
- Ensure all components are functional components with proper TypeScript typing.
- Use custom hooks for state management where appropriate.
- Optimize 3D scenes for performance in the browser.
- Ensure responsive design for different screen sizes.
- Place new components in the `frontend/src/components/` directory.
- Place 3D scenes in the `frontend/src/scenes/` directory.
- Use the `frontend/src/hooks/` directory for custom hooks.
- Use CSS modules or styled-components for styling, as per the project's convention.